---
// The Bridge. Datum's very first landing intro (datum-core eb8bbde, PR #446,
// July 2026): a scroll-scrubbed 3D film in which a cable-stayed river
// crossing surveys, drafts, builds, opens, and lights up with data, then
// dissolves into dawn. Retired two days later by the landing's rule against
// literal construction imagery. The film itself did nothing wrong.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const beats = [
  { kicker: 'Construction Intelligence', lines: ['Every build starts', 'from a single point.'] },
  { kicker: 'Plan', lines: ["First, it's lines on paper."] },
  { kicker: 'Build', lines: ['Then the field makes it real.'] },
  { kicker: 'Connect', lines: ['Datum keeps every beam, dollar,', 'and decision on one living record.'] },
  { kicker: 'Datum', lines: ['One company. One record.'], center: true },
];

const chips = [
  { id: 'report', label: 'Daily report filed', meta: 'Crew 12 · 5:58 AM' },
  { id: 'rfi', label: 'RFI #214 answered', meta: 'Ball in court · 2h' },
  { id: 'pour', label: 'Deck pour scheduled', meta: 'Span B3 · Thursday' },
  { id: 'payapp', label: 'Pay app #7 approved', meta: '$1.2M released' },
];
---

<Base
  title="The Bridge · Lab · Brett Boggs"
  description="A cable-stayed bridge that builds itself as you scroll. Datum's first landing film."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Lab · Jul 2026</p>
    <h1>The Bridge</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A river crossing that surveys, drafts, builds, and lights up as you scroll. Datum&rsquo;s
      first landing film.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="film-bleed">
    <p class="cin-sr">
      A night survey circles a glowing datum monument above a river valley. Blueprint lines draw
      a cable-stayed bridge in the air. Over a time-lapse day the field makes it real: pylons
      pour, deck segments hoist from the river, stay cables tension in. At dusk the lamps ignite,
      traffic crosses, and live project records pulse along the structure. Dawn blooms to white.
      Every build starts from a single point; Datum keeps every beam, dollar, and decision on one
      living record.
    </p>

    <div class="cin" data-film hidden>
      <div class="cin-stage">
        <canvas class="cin-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        <div class="cin-overlay" aria-hidden="true">
          {beats.map((b) => (
            <div class:list={['cin-beat', { 'cin-beat--center': b.center }]}>
              <div class="cin-kicker">{b.kicker}</div>
              <h2 class="cin-line">
                {b.lines.map((seg) => (
                  <span>{seg}<br /></span>
                ))}
              </h2>
            </div>
          ))}
          {chips.map((c) => (
            <div class="cin-chip" data-chip={c.id}>
              <span class="cin-chip-dot"></span>
              <div>
                <div class="cin-chip-label">{c.label}</div>
                <div class="cin-chip-meta">{c.meta}</div>
              </div>
              <span class="cin-chip-stem"></span>
            </div>
          ))}
          <div class="cin-brand">
            <span class="cin-wordmark">Datum</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cin-hint">
            <span>Scroll</span>
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6" /></svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="cin-skip">Skip film</button>
        <div class="cin-veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cin-unsupported" data-film-fallback>
      <p class="cin-kicker">Construction Intelligence</p>
      <p class="cin-line">Every build starts<br />from a single point.</p>
      <p class="cin-unsupported-note">
        The film needs WebGL2 and motion. This browser gets the title card instead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="colophon">
    <p>
      This was the very first opening film for datumci.com, v1 of what became a ten-version
      lineage. A night survey circles a glowing datum monument, blueprint lines draft a
      cable-stayed crossing in mid-air, and then a time-lapse day builds it for real: pylons
      slip-form upward, deck segments hoist off the river on lift lines, stay cables tension in,
      tower cranes work and dissolve. At dusk the lamps ignite and live project records pulse
      along the structure; dawn blooms to white. It lasted two days on the landing before the
      standing rule arrived that shaped every version after it: nothing literal, no construction
      imagery. The drafting film next door died on the same rule a few versions later.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pure three.js, and every mesh and texture is procedural; nothing is downloaded. PBR
      materials under an image-based environment, an animated sun with soft shadows, planar
      water reflections, ACES tone mapping, bloom, depth of field, and a film grade of grain,
      vignette, and chromatic aberration. The whole scene is a deterministic function of scroll
      progress, so scrolling back up un-builds the bridge. Phones get a lighter tier; browsers
      without WebGL2, or with reduced motion set, get the title card.
    </p>
  </div>

  <a class="back-link" href="/lab/">Back to Lab</a>
</Base>

<script>
  import { mountBridgeFilm, hasWebGL2 } from '../../scripts/bridgeFilm';

  const track = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-film]');
  const fallback = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-film-fallback]');
  const reduced = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  const supported = !reduced && hasWebGL2();

  if (track && supported) {
    track.hidden = false;
    if (fallback) fallback.style.display = 'none';
    mountBridgeFilm(track);
  }
</script>

<style>
  .film-bleed {
    width: 100vw;
    margin: 3rem 0 0 calc(50% - 50vw);
  }

  /* The film's palette, scoped. The render paints its own colors; these
     tokens style the overlay copy, the chips, and the one brand color the
     scene reads at runtime (the hologram azure, via --cta on the canvas). */
  .cin,
  .cin-unsupported {
    --bg-app: #070b12;
    --text-primary: #f2f5f7;
    --text-secondary: #c3cbd4;
    --text-muted: #8b95a3;
    --cta: #0a84ff;
    --glass-bg: rgba(10, 16, 26, 0.55);
    --border-subtle: rgba(242, 245, 247, 0.16);
    --border-strong: rgba(242, 245, 247, 0.4);
    --glass-blur: 12px;
    --radius-pill: 999px;
    --ease-out: var(--ease-warm);
    --font-display: var(--display);
    --font-body: var(--body);
    --font-crumb: var(--mono);
    --tracking-label: 0.16em;
    --tracking-display: -0.015em;
    --tracking-body-sm: 0.01em;
    --text-caption: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cin-sr {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: -1px;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  .cin {
    position: relative;
    height: 500vh; /* ~4 scroll-lengths of film + the release */
    background: var(--bg-app);
  }
  .cin[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .cin-stage {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    height: 100svh;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-app);
  }
  .cin-canvas {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.9s var(--ease-out);
  }
  .cin-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .cin-beat {
    position: absolute;
    left: clamp(24px, 7vw, 110px);
    bottom: clamp(72px, 16vh, 160px);
    max-width: 700px;
    opacity: 0;
    visibility: hidden;
  }
  .cin-beat--center {
    left: 50%;
    right: auto;
    bottom: auto;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .cin-beat--center .cin-line {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 62px);
  }
  .cin-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-crumb);
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .cin-line {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144, 'SOFT' 60, 'WONK' 1;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 50px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .cin-chip {
    position: absolute;
    transform: translate(-50%, calc(-100% - 26px));
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 9px;
    padding: 10px 14px 11px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur)) saturate(160%);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur)) saturate(160%);
    opacity: 0;
    visibility: hidden;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .cin-chip-dot {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--cta);
    margin-top: 5px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .cin-chip-label {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-body-sm);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .cin-chip-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-crumb);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .cin-chip-stem {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 100%;
    width: 1px;
    height: 26px;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--border-strong), transparent);
  }

  .cin-brand {
    position: absolute;
    top: 20px;
    left: 26px;
  }
  .cin-wordmark {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 21px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .cin-hint {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 22px;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-crumb);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .cin-hint svg {
    animation: cin-hint-bob 2.2s var(--ease-out) infinite;
  }
  @keyframes cin-hint-bob {
    0%,
    100% {
      transform: none;
    }
    50% {
      transform: translateY(4px);
    }
  }

  .cin-skip {
    position: absolute;
    top: 18px;
    right: 22px;
    z-index: 5;
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-body-sm);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      color 0.15s,
      border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .cin-skip:hover {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .cin-veil {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: var(--paper);
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Shown until the script confirms WebGL2 + motion; then the film takes over. */
  .cin-unsupported {
    background: var(--bg-app);
    padding: 18vh 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cin-unsupported .cin-line {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4.4vw, 54px);
  }
  .cin-unsupported-note {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cin-beat {
      bottom: 96px;
    }
    .cin-line {
      font-size: clamp(26px, 7.4vw, 38px);
    }
    .cin-chip {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
